# Citation metadata for bib (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# Validate with: uvx cffconvert --validate
# Replace the <placeholders> before tagging a release; keep in sync with
# .zenodo.json, pyproject.toml and src/bib/__init__.py.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use bib, please cite it using the metadata below and acknowledge the
  BPASS release papers listed under "references".
type: software
title: "bib — BPASS-in-Browser"
abstract: >-
  A pedagogical web explorer and REST API for BPASS (Binary Population and
  Spectral Synthesis) simple-stellar-population products: interactive SEDs,
  photon-weighted synthetic AB photometry through SVO filter curves, screen
  dust extinction within each law's validity window, redshifting with flat
  ΛCDM distances, and optional IGM attenuation (Inoue et al. 2014;
  Madau 1995), with per-filter flags stating what was applied.
version: 1.0.1
date-released: "2026-10-30"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Lyalpha/bib"
url: "https://bib.warwick.ac.uk"
keywords:
  - astronomy
  - BPASS
  - stellar populations
  - spectral synthesis
  - synthetic photometry
authors:
  - family-names: "Lyman"
    given-names: "J. D."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3464-0642"
    affiliation: "University of Warwick"
